# Local-only maintainer configuration. Keep this file untracked. Tracking it
# would put its contents into every archive built from this repository.
.publicdeny

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
.beads-credential-key

# The beads working directory, ignored whole — the beads repo itself does the
# same. Issue data lives in Dolt and travels as refs/dolt/data on the private
# origin, so nothing here is a source of truth: .beads/issues.jsonl is only an
# export, and the pre-commit hook rewrites it without staging it (export.auto
# is true, export.git-add is false). A fresh clone recovers with `bd bootstrap`,
# which wires the origin itself once it finds refs/dolt/data.
#
# This also puts each beads file behind the *first* publish gate.
# scripts/publish-public.sh builds its tree with `git archive`, so an untracked
# file cannot reach the mirror at all. .publicignore keeps its entry as the
# second gate — see docs/private-operations.md.
#
# "`.beads/*`", not "`.beads/`": git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so the directory form would make a later negation such as
# "`!.beads/formulas/`" silently do nothing.
.beads/*
